<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia31fb7eebe562b36216ce547c9889bcffba7f257" commit="2c1e14ecc875d0f759fbbdf9146d0de27148ba61" commit_message="libcontainer: Separate cgroup configuration from creation  This adds the ability to set the owner of the parent cgroups, this is needed when entering a cgroup namespace as the subdirectories and their files must be owned by the user that root maps to outside the container. Move cgroup creation from where the config is created until later.  This information isn't known by login manager when creating the container. Moving it later allows it to be configured like other config options.  BUG=none TEST=run with dependent changes and see that the cgroup is created with the correct owner and at the correct place in the cgroup hierarchy.  Change-Id: Ia31fb7eebe562b36216ce547c9889bcffba7f257 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362097 Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="362097" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/97/362097/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic361c2cf0904d05b959fad51c53b2fd983b22bc9" commit="67b8939ba29dedba7cc2d8aa85c4c1e1d0553179" commit_message="login: Set cgroup parent directory for android containers  Android will now run in a new cgroup namespace.  This will allow it to modify its own cgroups while not knowing that it is part of a larger cgroup hierarchy.  Configure the external cgroup &quot;session_manager_containers&quot; that will be the root of Android's cgroup namespace.  BUG=b/29259708 TEST=Start android and check that it is in a new cgroup namespace rooted at session_manager_containers.  Change-Id: Ic361c2cf0904d05b959fad51c53b2fd983b22bc9 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362099 Reviewed-by: Dan Erat (OOO 8-12 to 8-22) &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="362099" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/99/362099/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I83e93ea6135f2b3f4baa4816eacacd1e02f1986a" commit="1570bcaf742fe8ac6d82ce493261af9d60260f66" commit_message="libcontainer: Run containers in a cgroup namespace  Now that all of our supported kernels support cgroup namespaces, enable them when running a container.  This will allow the container to modify cgroup parameters for sub groups but still allows the system to control overall limits.  The contained processes will not know that it is in a cgroup namespace, it appears as the root inside the namespace.  BUG=b/29259708 TEST=boot android on cyan and check cgroup membership inside and outside the container.  Change-Id: I83e93ea6135f2b3f4baa4816eacacd1e02f1986a Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362350 " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="362350" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/50/362350/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I852132ee8cd67063921077cd0b7d848d10a730e0" commit="246bed4cea712789582b2fac4e9774ba999d8d81" commit_message="math_util: Fix rotation by identity.  Rotation by identity matrix from a to b fails if a != b.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=Use identity matrix in test motion_lid.c, check test passes.  Change-Id: I852132ee8cd67063921077cd0b7d848d10a730e0 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://c